WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.669
Hi, and welcome to Fabric!

2
00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:04.880
In the next two minutes,

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.093
I'll show you how Fabric turns everyday conversations about your work…

4
00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:11.320
into clear, living process maps,

5
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:13.530
and practical ways to improve them.

6
00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:17.252
This is your workspace.

7
00:00:17.252 --> 00:00:19.572
On the left is the Process Tree:

8
00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:22.542
your organization, laid out as functions,

9
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:25.292
departments, and the processes inside them.

10
00:00:25.292 --> 00:00:27.452
Click to expand any branch…

11
00:00:27.452 --> 00:00:31.422
or press Control K to jump straight to a process by name.

12
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.516
Every process has its own page,

13
00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:36.830
and this is where it all starts.

14
00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.550
Hit Start AI interview,

15
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.630
and Fabric's voice agent will talk you through how the work really gets done:

16
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.190
the steps, the tools,

17
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:45.407
the handoffs.

18
00:00:45.407 --> 00:00:46.790
Prefer to go solo?

19
00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:47.790
Record a voice note,

20
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.240
or upload a recording you already have.

21
00:00:50.786 --> 00:00:53.746
Every interview lands in the Contributions tab,

22
00:00:53.746 --> 00:00:55.866
with the audio, an AI summary,

23
00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:59.036
and a full transcript you can read and replay.

24
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:02.093
Now here's where it gets interesting.

25
00:01:02.323 --> 00:01:07.563
Fabric reads across every contribution and writes a single overview of the process:

26
00:01:07.563 --> 00:01:09.163
the key facts up top,

27
00:01:09.163 --> 00:01:10.640
then the full story.

28
00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:13.683
Further down, it shows where people agree,

29
00:01:13.683 --> 00:01:15.283
where their accounts differ…

30
00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:17.643
and which sources back up each point.

31
00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:19.243
The more people you interview,

32
00:01:19.243 --> 00:01:21.133
the sharper the picture gets.

33
00:01:21.691 --> 00:01:25.051
Open Process Flow to see it all as a map:

34
00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.811
every step, decision, and handoff,

35
00:01:27.811 --> 00:01:30.171
built from what people actually said.

36
00:01:30.171 --> 00:01:32.411
Bottlenecks are flagged right on the steps,

37
00:01:32.411 --> 00:01:34.901
so you can spot the friction at a glance.

38
00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:38.004
Insights starts with key findings:

39
00:01:38.004 --> 00:01:40.471
the places worth a closer look.

40
00:01:40.471 --> 00:01:43.551
Then it rolls everything up into the numbers:

41
00:01:43.551 --> 00:01:46.231
steps, handoffs, tools, decisions,

42
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:49.801
and bottlenecks, each traced back to the evidence.

43
00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:53.069
And finally, Recommendations:

44
00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:54.999
what to change, and why.

45
00:01:55.309 --> 00:01:57.629
Fabric suggests practical fixes,

46
00:01:57.629 --> 00:02:00.589
from a clear handover rule to a new workflow,

47
00:02:00.589 --> 00:02:02.629
each ranked by value and effort,

48
00:02:02.629 --> 00:02:05.199
and backed by what people actually said.

49
00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:08.469
Every recommendation comes with a small pilot to try…

50
00:02:08.469 --> 00:02:11.879
and a change plan you can copy and share with your team.

51
00:02:12.675 --> 00:02:14.115
So that's Fabric.

52
00:02:14.115 --> 00:02:15.915
Pick a process you know well,

53
00:02:15.915 --> 00:02:17.675
hit Start AI interview,

54
00:02:17.675 --> 00:02:18.904
and just talk.

55
00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.525
We'll take care of the rest!
